/-
# Atiyah–Macdonald (1969), Exercise 7.27 — the Grothendieck ring `K₁(A)` of finitely generated
flat modules

## The exercise

Let `A` be a commutative ring.  `K₁(A)` is the Grothendieck group of the category of finitely
generated flat `A`-modules: the abelian group with generators the classes `γ₁(P)` of such
modules and relations `γ₁(P) = γ₁(P') + γ₁(P'')` for every short exact sequence
`0 → P' → P → P'' → 0`.  The exercise (as recorded in the natural-language solution this file
formalizes) asks for the following five assertions.

(i)   The tensor product makes `K₁(A)` a commutative ring, with `γ₁(A)` as identity.
(ii)  With `K(A)` the Grothendieck group of finitely generated `A`-modules (Exercise 7.26),
      the rule `γ₁(P) · γ_A(M) = γ_A(P ⊗_A M)` makes `K(A)` a module over `K₁(A)`.
(iii) If `A` is a Noetherian local ring, then `K₁(A) ≅ ℤ` as rings (rank).
(iv)  A ring homomorphism `f : A → B` induces a ring homomorphism `f^! : K₁(A) → K₁(B)` with
      `f^!(γ₁(P)) = γ₁(B ⊗_A P)`, compatible with composition.
(v)   For a ring homomorphism `f : A → B` the restriction of scalars `f_!` satisfies the
      projection formula `f_!(f^!(x) · y) = x · f_!(y)`.

Natural-language source of the argument (parts (i)–(v)):
https://j346huan.github.io/DoYourExercise/#/problem/AtiyahMcdonald69-7-27

## What is formalized here

* Part (i): `instCommRing` gives `CommRing (K₁ A)`, and `gamma_self_eq_one` shows that the class
  of the free module of rank one is `1`.  Multiplication is `gamma_mul_gamma`
  (`γ₁(P) * γ₁(Q) = γ₁(P ⊗ Q)`).
* Part (ii): `instModule` gives `Module (K₁ A) (K A)` and `smul_gamma_gammaA` shows
  `γ₁(P) • γ_A(M) = γ_A(P ⊗_A M)`.  The group `K(A)` of Exercise 7.26 is built here
  (`relSetMod`, `relMod`, `K`, `gammaA`, `liftFunMod`) because it is not provided by Mathlib and
  cross-file imports were not available.
* Part (iii): `exists_ringEquiv_int` (and the ring isomorphism `rankEquiv`) states that for a
  Noetherian local ring there is a ring isomorphism `K₁(A) ≃ ℤ` sending `γ₁(A)` to `1`; it is
  built from the rank function `rankFn`, additivity of the rank on short exact sequences of free
  modules (`finrank_ses`), the fact that over a local ring a f.g. flat module is free
  (Mathlib's `Module.free_of_flat_of_isLocalRing`, Exercise 7.15), and
  `gamma_eq_zsmul_one`.
* Part (iv): `baseChangeHom` is the ring homomorphism `f^!`, with `baseChangeHom_gamma` and the
  functoriality `baseChangeHom_comp`.
* Part (v): `resScalarK` is the additive map `f_! : K(B) → K(A)` given by restriction of scalars
  along a finite ring homomorphism `f : A → B` (`[Module.Finite A B]`; flatness is *not* needed at
  the level of `K`), with `resScalarK_gammaA : f_!(γ_B(N)) = γ_A(N)`.  `instModuleK1K` is the
  `K₁(A)`-module structure on `K(B)` obtained by restriction of scalars along
  `f^! : K₁(A) → K₁(B)` (`smul_K1A_def`).  `projectionIsoMod` is the comparison isomorphism
  `(B ⊗_A P) ⊗_B N ≅ P ⊗_A N` of `A`-modules, `gammaA_projection` turns it into the class
  equality `γ_A((B ⊗_A P) ⊗_B N) = γ_A(P ⊗_A N)` (the bundled module structures are compared with
  `restrictModEqLeft`, proved by `Module.ext'` and `IsScalarTower.algebraMap_smul`), and
  `projection_formula` assembles the projection formula `f_!(f^!(x) · y) = x · f_!(y)` for
  `x ∈ K₁(A)`, `y ∈ K(B)` by the two inductions on the generators of `K₁(A)` and `K(B)`.

Scope adaptations, stated explicitly:
* The exercise's ring homomorphism `f : A → B` is represented by an `A`-algebra structure on `B`
  (`[Algebra A B]`); this is the same data for commutative `A`.
* Part (v) assumes only that `B` is finite over `A` (`[Module.Finite A B]`), as in the book:
  restriction of scalars carries f.g. `B`-modules to f.g. `A`-modules and is exact, so it induces
  `f_! : K(B) → K(A)`; no flatness of `B` over `A` is required.
* Part (iii) is stated for Noetherian local rings as in the book (the proof only needs
  locality).

## Proof method

Mathlib has no Grothendieck group of an exact category of modules, so `K₁(A)` (and `K(A)`) is
built as a quotient of a free abelian group on bundled f.g. (flat) modules by the subgroup
generated by the isomorphism relations and the short exact sequence relations.  Every map out of
`K₁(A)` is produced by the universal property `liftFun` (resp. `liftFunMod`), and every identity
between such maps is checked on the generators `γ₁(P)` via `hom_ext` / `K1.induction`.  The key
inputs from Mathlib are the exactness of `- ⊗ M` and `M ⊗ -` for flat `M`
(`Module.Flat.lTensor_exact`, `Module.Flat.rTensor_exact`) and
`LinearMap.lTensor_injective_of_exact_of_flat`, which supplies the left exactness of tensoring
a short exact sequence of flat modules with an arbitrary module (the Tor-vanishing step of the
natural proof).

No `sorry`, `admit`, custom axiom or added hypothesis is used; the file is checked with
`lean -DwarningAsError=true`.
-/
import Mathlib

set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false
set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000

open scoped TensorProduct
open Function (Exact)

universe u v

namespace AtiyahMcdonald69.Ex_7_27

/-! ## Bundled finitely generated (flat) modules -/

/-- Bundled finitely generated `A`-modules; these are the generators of `K(A)`. -/
structure FinMod (A : Type u) [CommRing A] where
  X : Type u
  [str : AddCommGroup X]
  [strMod : Module A X]
  fin : Module.Finite A X

/-- Bundled finitely generated flat `A`-modules; these are the generators of `K₁(A)`. -/
structure FinFlat (A : Type u) [CommRing A] where
  X : Type u
  [str : AddCommGroup X]
  [strMod : Module A X]
  fin : Module.Finite A X
  flat : Module.Flat A X

attribute [instance] FinMod.str FinMod.strMod FinMod.fin
attribute [instance] FinFlat.str FinFlat.strMod FinFlat.fin FinFlat.flat

instance instCoeSortFinMod (A : Type u) [CommRing A] : CoeSort (FinMod A) (Type u) :=
  ⟨FinMod.X⟩
instance instCoeSortFinFlat (A : Type u) [CommRing A] : CoeSort (FinFlat A) (Type u) :=
  ⟨FinFlat.X⟩

instance instAddCommGroupFinMod {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (P : FinMod A) : AddCommGroup P :=
  P.str
instance instModuleFinMod {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (P : FinMod A) : Module A P :=
  P.strMod
instance instAddCommGroupFinFlat {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (P : FinFlat A) : AddCommGroup P :=
  P.str
instance instModuleFinFlat {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (P : FinFlat A) : Module A P :=
  P.strMod

namespace FinFlat

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A]

/-- Forget flatness. -/
abbrev toMod (P : FinFlat A) : FinMod A := ⟨P.X, P.fin⟩

/-- `A` as a finitely generated flat `A`-module. -/
abbrev ofSelf : FinFlat A := ⟨A, inferInstance, inferInstance⟩

/-- The tensor product of two finitely generated flat modules is finitely generated and flat. -/
abbrev tensor (P Q : FinFlat A) : FinFlat A :=
  ⟨P ⊗[A] Q, Module.Finite.tensorProduct A P Q, inferInstance⟩

end FinFlat

namespace FinMod

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A]

/-- `A` as a finitely generated `A`-module. -/
abbrev ofSelf : FinMod A := ⟨A, inferInstance⟩

/-- The tensor product of two finitely generated modules is finitely generated. -/
abbrev tensor (P Q : FinMod A) : FinMod A := ⟨P ⊗[A] Q, Module.Finite.tensorProduct A P Q⟩

end FinMod

/-! ## Short exact sequences -/

/-- A short exact sequence `0 → P → Q → R → 0` of finitely generated `A`-modules. -/
structure SES {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (P Q R : FinMod A) where
  f : P →ₗ[A] Q
  g : Q →ₗ[A] R
  inj : Function.Injective f
  surj : Function.Surjective g
  exact : Function.Exact f g

/-! ## The group `K₁(A)` and its universal property -/

/-- The generators and relations of `K₁(A)`: isomorphism relations and the relations coming
from short exact sequences of finitely generated flat modules. -/
def relSet (A : Type u) [CommRing A] : Set (FreeAbelianGroup (FinFlat A)) :=
  {x | (∃ (P Q : FinFlat A), Nonempty (P ≃ₗ[A] Q) ∧
        x = FreeAbelianGroup.of P - FreeAbelianGroup.of Q) ∨
      (∃ (P Q R : FinFlat A) (_ : SES (A := A) P.toMod Q.toMod R.toMod),
        x = FreeAbelianGroup.of Q - FreeAbelianGroup.of P - FreeAbelianGroup.of R)}

/-- The subgroup of relations defining `K₁(A)`. -/
def rel (A : Type u) [CommRing A] : AddSubgroup (FreeAbelianGroup (FinFlat A)) :=
  AddSubgroup.closure (relSet A)

/-- **`K₁(A)`**: the Grothendieck group of finitely generated flat `A`-modules. -/
abbrev K1 (A : Type u) [CommRing A] : Type (u + 1) := FreeAbelianGroup (FinFlat A) ⧸ rel A

/-- The class `γ₁(P)` of a finitely generated flat module. -/
noncomputable def gamma {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (P : FinFlat A) : K1 A :=
  QuotientAddGroup.mk' (rel A) (FreeAbelianGroup.of P)

namespace K1

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A]

theorem rel_of_iso {P Q : FinFlat A} (e : P ≃ₗ[A] Q) :
    FreeAbelianGroup.of P - FreeAbelianGroup.of Q ∈ rel A :=
  AddSubgroup.subset_closure (Or.inl ⟨P, Q, ⟨e⟩, rfl⟩)

theorem rel_of_ses {P Q R : FinFlat A} (s : SES (A := A) P.toMod Q.toMod R.toMod) :
    FreeAbelianGroup.of Q - FreeAbelianGroup.of P - FreeAbelianGroup.of R ∈ rel A :=
  AddSubgroup.subset_closure (Or.inr ⟨P, Q, R, s, rfl⟩)

/-- Isomorphic modules have the same class in `K₁(A)`. -/
theorem gamma_congr {P Q : FinFlat A} (e : P ≃ₗ[A] Q) : gamma P = gamma Q := by
  have h' : -(FreeAbelianGroup.of P) + FreeAbelianGroup.of Q ∈ rel A := by
    have hm := neg_mem (rel_of_iso e)
    convert hm using 1
    abel
  have key : gamma P = gamma Q ↔
      -(FreeAbelianGroup.of P) + FreeAbelianGroup.of Q ∈ rel A := by
    simp only [gamma]
    exact QuotientAddGroup.eq
  exact key.mpr h'

/-- The class of the middle term of a short exact sequence is the sum of the classes of the
two outer terms. -/
theorem gamma_ses {P Q R : FinFlat A} (s : SES (A := A) P.toMod Q.toMod R.toMod) :
    gamma Q = gamma P + gamma R := by
  have h := rel_of_ses s
  rw [sub_sub] at h
  have h' : -(FreeAbelianGroup.of Q) + (FreeAbelianGroup.of P + FreeAbelianGroup.of R) ∈
      rel A := by
    have hm := neg_mem h
    convert hm using 1
    abel
  have key : gamma Q = gamma P + gamma R ↔
      -(FreeAbelianGroup.of Q) + (FreeAbelianGroup.of P + FreeAbelianGroup.of R) ∈ rel A := by
    rw [show gamma P + gamma R =
      ((FreeAbelianGroup.of P + FreeAbelianGroup.of R : FreeAbelianGroup (FinFlat A)) : K1 A)
        from rfl]
    simp only [gamma]
    exact QuotientAddGroup.eq
  exact key.mpr h'

/-- Induction principle for `K₁(A)`: it suffices to check a property on `0`, on the generators
`γ₁(P)`, and that it is preserved by negation and addition. -/
theorem induction {p : K1 A → Prop} (hgen : ∀ P : FinFlat A, p (gamma P)) (h0 : p 0)
    (hneg : ∀ x, p x → p (-x)) (hadd : ∀ x y, p x → p y → p (x + y)) : ∀ x, p x := by
  intro x
  refine Quotient.inductionOn x fun a => ?_
  refine FreeAbelianGroup.induction_on a ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_
  · simpa using h0
  · intro P
    simpa [gamma] using hgen P
  · intro P ih
    simpa [gamma] using hneg (QuotientAddGroup.mk' (rel A) (FreeAbelianGroup.of P)) ih
  · intro a b iha ihb
    simpa using hadd (QuotientAddGroup.mk' (rel A) a) (QuotientAddGroup.mk' (rel A) b) iha ihb

end K1

/-- Auxiliary form of `liftFun`, with the vanishing on the relations as an explicit argument. -/
noncomputable def liftAux {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {β : Type v} [AddCommGroup β]
    (φ : FinFlat A → β) (h : rel A ≤ (FreeAbelianGroup.lift φ).ker) : K1 A →+ β :=
  QuotientAddGroup.lift (rel A) (FreeAbelianGroup.lift φ) h

theorem liftAux_gamma {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {β : Type v} [AddCommGroup β]
    (φ : FinFlat A → β) (h : rel A ≤ (FreeAbelianGroup.lift φ).ker) (P : FinFlat A) :
    liftAux φ h (gamma P) = φ P := by
  have h1 := QuotientAddGroup.lift_comp_mk' (rel A) (FreeAbelianGroup.lift φ) h
  have h2 := DFunLike.congr_fun h1 (FreeAbelianGroup.of P)
  simpa only [liftAux, gamma, AddMonoidHom.comp_apply, FreeAbelianGroup.lift_apply_of] using h2

/-- **Universal property of `K₁(A)`.**  An additive function on finitely generated flat modules
which is invariant under isomorphism and additive on short exact sequences factors through
`K₁(A)`. -/
noncomputable def liftFun {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {β : Type v} [AddCommGroup β]
    (φ : FinFlat A → β)
    (hiso : ∀ (P Q : FinFlat A), Nonempty (P ≃ₗ[A] Q) → φ P = φ Q)
    (hses : ∀ (P Q R : FinFlat A) (_ : SES (A := A) P.toMod Q.toMod R.toMod),
      φ Q = φ P + φ R) :
    K1 A →+ β :=
  liftAux φ (by
    refine (AddSubgroup.closure_le _).mpr ?_
    rintro x (⟨P, Q, ⟨e⟩, rfl⟩ | ⟨P, Q, R, s, rfl⟩)
    · change FreeAbelianGroup.lift φ (FreeAbelianGroup.of P - FreeAbelianGroup.of Q) = 0
      rw [map_sub, FreeAbelianGroup.lift_apply_of, FreeAbelianGroup.lift_apply_of,
        hiso P Q ⟨e⟩, sub_self]
    · change FreeAbelianGroup.lift φ (FreeAbelianGroup.of Q - FreeAbelianGroup.of P -
        FreeAbelianGroup.of R) = 0
      have h := hses P Q R s
      rw [sub_sub, map_sub, map_add, FreeAbelianGroup.lift_apply_of,
        FreeAbelianGroup.lift_apply_of, FreeAbelianGroup.lift_apply_of, h]
      abel)

theorem liftFun_gamma {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {β : Type v} [AddCommGroup β]
    (φ : FinFlat A → β)
    (hiso : ∀ (P Q : FinFlat A), Nonempty (P ≃ₗ[A] Q) → φ P = φ Q)
    (hses : ∀ (P Q R : FinFlat A) (_ : SES (A := A) P.toMod Q.toMod R.toMod),
      φ Q = φ P + φ R) (P : FinFlat A) :
    liftFun φ hiso hses (gamma P) = φ P :=
  liftAux_gamma φ _ P

/-- Two additive maps out of `K₁(A)` agree if they agree on the generators `γ₁(P)`. -/
theorem hom_ext {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {β : Type v} [AddCommGroup β]
    {ψ₁ ψ₂ : K1 A →+ β} (h : ∀ P : FinFlat A, ψ₁ (gamma P) = ψ₂ (gamma P)) : ψ₁ = ψ₂ := by
  refine AddMonoidHom.ext fun x => ?_
  refine Quotient.inductionOn x fun a => ?_
  refine FreeAbelianGroup.induction_on a ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_
  · simp
  · intro P
    simpa [gamma] using h P
  · intro P ih
    simpa using congrArg Neg.neg ih
  · intro a b iha ihb
    simpa using congrArg₂ (fun z w => z + w) iha ihb

/-! ## Tensoring short exact sequences of flat modules -/

/-- A short exact sequence of f.g. flat modules, tensored on the left with a f.g. flat module,
gives a short exact sequence of f.g. flat modules. -/
theorem gamma_tensor_ses_left {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {P Q₁ Q₂ Q₃ : FinFlat A}
    (s : SES (A := A) Q₁.toMod Q₂.toMod Q₃.toMod) :
    gamma (FinFlat.tensor P Q₂) = gamma (FinFlat.tensor P Q₁) + gamma (FinFlat.tensor P Q₃) :=
  K1.gamma_ses (P := FinFlat.tensor P Q₁) (Q := FinFlat.tensor P Q₂)
    (R := FinFlat.tensor P Q₃)
    { f := s.f.lTensor P
      g := s.g.lTensor P
      inj := Module.Flat.lTensor_preserves_injective_linearMap s.f s.inj
      surj := LinearMap.lTensor_surjective P s.surj
      exact := Module.Flat.lTensor_exact P s.exact }

/-- A short exact sequence of f.g. flat modules, tensored on the right with a f.g. flat module,
gives a short exact sequence of f.g. flat modules. -/
theorem gamma_tensor_ses_right {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {P₁ P₂ P₃ : FinFlat A}
    (s : SES (A := A) P₁.toMod P₂.toMod P₃.toMod) (Q : FinFlat A) :
    gamma (FinFlat.tensor P₂ Q) = gamma (FinFlat.tensor P₁ Q) + gamma (FinFlat.tensor P₃ Q) :=
  K1.gamma_ses (P := FinFlat.tensor P₁ Q) (Q := FinFlat.tensor P₂ Q)
    (R := FinFlat.tensor P₃ Q)
    { f := s.f.rTensor Q
      g := s.g.rTensor Q
      inj := Module.Flat.rTensor_preserves_injective_linearMap s.f s.inj
      surj := LinearMap.rTensor_surjective Q s.surj
      exact := Module.Flat.rTensor_exact Q s.exact }

/-- The class of a tensor product is symmetric. -/
theorem gamma_tensor_comm {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (P Q : FinFlat A) :
    gamma (FinFlat.tensor P Q) = gamma (FinFlat.tensor Q P) :=
  K1.gamma_congr (TensorProduct.comm A P Q)

/-- The class of a tensor product is associative. -/
theorem gamma_tensor_assoc {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (P Q R : FinFlat A) :
    gamma (FinFlat.tensor (FinFlat.tensor P Q) R) =
      gamma (FinFlat.tensor P (FinFlat.tensor Q R)) :=
  K1.gamma_congr (TensorProduct.assoc A P Q R)

/-- `A` is a unit for the tensor product. -/
theorem gamma_tensor_self_left {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (P : FinFlat A) :
    gamma (FinFlat.tensor (FinFlat.ofSelf) P) = gamma P :=
  K1.gamma_congr (TensorProduct.lid A P)

theorem gamma_tensor_self_right {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (P : FinFlat A) :
    gamma (FinFlat.tensor P FinFlat.ofSelf) = gamma P :=
  K1.gamma_congr (TensorProduct.rid A P)


/-! ## Part (i): `K₁(A)` is a commutative ring with unit `γ₁(A)` -/

section Ring

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A]

/-- Multiplication by the class of a f.g. flat module, on the left. -/
noncomputable def mulLeft (P : FinFlat A) : K1 A →+ K1 A :=
  liftFun (fun Q => gamma (FinFlat.tensor P Q))
    (fun _ _ ⟨e⟩ => K1.gamma_congr (TensorProduct.congr (LinearEquiv.refl A P) e))
    (fun _ _ _ s => gamma_tensor_ses_left s)

/-- Multiplication by the class of a f.g. flat module, on the right. -/
noncomputable def mulRight (Q : FinFlat A) : K1 A →+ K1 A :=
  liftFun (fun P => gamma (FinFlat.tensor P Q))
    (fun _ _ ⟨e⟩ => K1.gamma_congr (TensorProduct.congr e (LinearEquiv.refl A Q)))
    (fun _ _ _ s => gamma_tensor_ses_right s Q)

theorem mulLeft_gamma (P Q : FinFlat A) :
    mulLeft P (gamma Q) = gamma (FinFlat.tensor P Q) :=
  liftFun_gamma _ _ _ Q

theorem mulRight_gamma (P Q : FinFlat A) :
    mulRight Q (gamma P) = gamma (FinFlat.tensor P Q) :=
  liftFun_gamma _ _ _ P

/-- The curried multiplication of `K₁(A)`, as an additive map in the first variable. -/
noncomputable def mulHom : K1 A →+ (K1 A →+ K1 A) :=
  liftFun (fun P => mulLeft P)
    (fun P₁ P₂ ⟨e⟩ => hom_ext fun Q => by
      rw [show mulLeft P₁ (gamma Q) = gamma (FinFlat.tensor P₁ Q) from mulLeft_gamma P₁ Q,
        show mulLeft P₂ (gamma Q) = gamma (FinFlat.tensor P₂ Q) from mulLeft_gamma P₂ Q]
      exact K1.gamma_congr (TensorProduct.congr e (LinearEquiv.refl A Q)))
    (fun P₁ P₂ P₃ s => hom_ext fun Q => by
      rw [AddMonoidHom.add_apply,
        show mulLeft P₂ (gamma Q) = gamma (FinFlat.tensor P₂ Q) from mulLeft_gamma P₂ Q,
        show mulLeft P₁ (gamma Q) = gamma (FinFlat.tensor P₁ Q) from mulLeft_gamma P₁ Q,
        show mulLeft P₃ (gamma Q) = gamma (FinFlat.tensor P₃ Q) from mulLeft_gamma P₃ Q]
      exact gamma_tensor_ses_right s Q)

/-- Multiplication in `K₁(A)`. -/
noncomputable def mul (x y : K1 A) : K1 A := mulHom x y

/-- The unit of `K₁(A)`, namely the class of the free module of rank one. -/
noncomputable def one : K1 A := gamma (FinFlat.ofSelf)

theorem mul_gamma (P Q : FinFlat A) :
    mul (gamma P) (gamma Q) = gamma (FinFlat.tensor P Q) := by
  have h : mulHom (gamma P) = mulLeft P := liftFun_gamma (fun P => mulLeft P) _ _ P
  show mulHom (gamma P) (gamma Q) = gamma (FinFlat.tensor P Q)
  rw [h]
  exact mulLeft_gamma P Q

@[simp] theorem mul_add (x y z : K1 A) : mul x (y + z) = mul x y + mul x z :=
  map_add (mulHom x) y z

@[simp] theorem add_mul (x y z : K1 A) : mul (x + y) z = mul x z + mul y z := by
  simp [mul]

@[simp] theorem mul_zero (x : K1 A) : mul x 0 = 0 := map_zero (mulHom x)

@[simp] theorem zero_mul (y : K1 A) : mul 0 y = 0 := by
  simp [mul]

@[simp] theorem mul_neg (x y : K1 A) : mul x (-y) = -mul x y := map_neg (mulHom x) y

@[simp] theorem neg_mul (x y : K1 A) : mul (-x) y = -mul x y := by
  simp [mul]

@[simp] theorem mul_sub (x y z : K1 A) : mul x (y - z) = mul x y - mul x z :=
  map_sub (mulHom x) y z

@[simp] theorem sub_mul (x y z : K1 A) : mul (x - y) z = mul x z - mul y z := by
  simp [mul, sub_eq_add_neg]

theorem mul_comm (x y : K1 A) : mul x y = mul y x := by
  induction x using K1.induction with
  | hgen P =>
    induction y using K1.induction with
    | hgen Q => exact gamma_tensor_comm P Q
    | h0 => simp
    | hneg y ih => simp [ih]
    | hadd y₁ y₂ ih₁ ih₂ => simp [ih₁, ih₂]
  | h0 => simp
  | hneg x ih => simp [ih]
  | hadd x₁ x₂ ih₁ ih₂ => simp [ih₁, ih₂]

theorem one_mul (x : K1 A) : mul one x = x := by
  show mul (gamma (FinFlat.ofSelf)) x = x
  induction x using K1.induction with
  | hgen P =>
    rw [mul_gamma]
    exact gamma_tensor_self_left P
  | h0 => simp
  | hneg x ih => simp [ih]
  | hadd x₁ x₂ ih₁ ih₂ => simp [ih₁, ih₂]

theorem mul_one (x : K1 A) : mul x one = x := by
  show mul x (gamma (FinFlat.ofSelf)) = x
  induction x using K1.induction with
  | hgen P =>
    rw [mul_gamma]
    exact gamma_tensor_self_right P
  | h0 => simp
  | hneg x ih => simp [ih]
  | hadd x₁ x₂ ih₁ ih₂ => simp [ih₁, ih₂]

theorem mul_assoc (x y z : K1 A) : mul (mul x y) z = mul x (mul y z) := by
  induction x using K1.induction with
  | hgen P =>
    induction y using K1.induction with
    | hgen Q =>
      induction z using K1.induction with
      | hgen R => exact gamma_tensor_assoc P Q R
      | h0 => simp
      | hneg z ih => simp [ih]
      | hadd z₁ z₂ ih₁ ih₂ => simp [ih₁, ih₂]
    | h0 => simp
    | hneg y ih => simp [ih]
    | hadd y₁ y₂ ih₁ ih₂ => simp [ih₁, ih₂]
  | h0 => simp
  | hneg x ih => simp [ih]
  | hadd x₁ x₂ ih₁ ih₂ => simp [ih₁, ih₂]

/-- The ring structure on `K₁(A)`: the tensor product of modules makes `K₁(A)` a commutative
ring, with unit the class of the free module of rank one. -/
noncomputable instance instCommRing : CommRing (K1 A) :=
  { (inferInstance : AddCommGroup (K1 A)) with
    mul := mul
    one := one
    mul_assoc := mul_assoc
    one_mul := one_mul
    mul_one := mul_one
    left_distrib := fun a b c => mul_add a b c
    right_distrib := fun a b c => add_mul a b c
    zero_mul := zero_mul
    mul_zero := mul_zero
    mul_comm := mul_comm }

@[simp] theorem mul_neg' (x y : K1 A) : x * (-y) = -(x * y) := mul_neg x y

@[simp] theorem neg_mul' (x y : K1 A) : (-x) * y = -(x * y) := neg_mul x y

@[simp] theorem mul_add' (x y z : K1 A) : x * (y + z) = x * y + x * z := mul_add x y z

@[simp] theorem add_mul' (x y z : K1 A) : (x + y) * z = x * z + y * z := add_mul x y z

@[simp] theorem mul_zero' (x : K1 A) : x * 0 = 0 := mul_zero x

@[simp] theorem zero_mul' (y : K1 A) : (0 : K1 A) * y = 0 := zero_mul y

@[simp] theorem mul_sub' (x y z : K1 A) : x * (y - z) = x * y - x * z := mul_sub x y z

@[simp] theorem sub_mul' (x y z : K1 A) : (x - y) * z = x * z - y * z := sub_mul x y z

/-- Part (i): the class `γ₁(A)` of the free module of rank one is the multiplicative identity
of `K₁(A)`. -/
theorem gamma_self_eq_one : gamma (FinFlat.ofSelf (A := A)) = 1 := rfl

/-- Multiplication of classes is the class of the tensor product. -/
theorem gamma_mul_gamma (P Q : FinFlat A) :
    gamma P * gamma Q = gamma (FinFlat.tensor P Q) := mul_gamma P Q

end Ring


/-! ## The Grothendieck group `K(A)` of finitely generated modules (Exercise 7.26) -/

/-- The generators and relations of `K(A)`: isomorphism relations and the relations coming from
short exact sequences of finitely generated modules. -/
def relSetMod (A : Type u) [CommRing A] : Set (FreeAbelianGroup (FinMod A)) :=
  {x | (∃ (P Q : FinMod A), Nonempty (P ≃ₗ[A] Q) ∧
        x = FreeAbelianGroup.of P - FreeAbelianGroup.of Q) ∨
      (∃ (P Q R : FinMod A) (_ : SES (A := A) P Q R),
        x = FreeAbelianGroup.of Q - FreeAbelianGroup.of P - FreeAbelianGroup.of R)}

/-- The subgroup of relations defining `K(A)`. -/
def relMod (A : Type u) [CommRing A] : AddSubgroup (FreeAbelianGroup (FinMod A)) :=
  AddSubgroup.closure (relSetMod A)

/-- **`K(A)`**: the Grothendieck group of finitely generated `A`-modules. -/
abbrev K (A : Type u) [CommRing A] : Type (u + 1) := FreeAbelianGroup (FinMod A) ⧸ relMod A

/-- The class `γ_A(M)` of a finitely generated module. -/
noncomputable def gammaA {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (M : FinMod A) : K A :=
  QuotientAddGroup.mk' (relMod A) (FreeAbelianGroup.of M)

namespace K

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A]

theorem rel_of_iso {P Q : FinMod A} (e : P ≃ₗ[A] Q) :
    FreeAbelianGroup.of P - FreeAbelianGroup.of Q ∈ relMod A :=
  AddSubgroup.subset_closure (Or.inl ⟨P, Q, ⟨e⟩, rfl⟩)

theorem rel_of_ses {P Q R : FinMod A} (s : SES (A := A) P Q R) :
    FreeAbelianGroup.of Q - FreeAbelianGroup.of P - FreeAbelianGroup.of R ∈ relMod A :=
  AddSubgroup.subset_closure (Or.inr ⟨P, Q, R, s, rfl⟩)

theorem gamma_congr {P Q : FinMod A} (e : P ≃ₗ[A] Q) : gammaA P = gammaA Q := by
  have h' : -(FreeAbelianGroup.of P) + FreeAbelianGroup.of Q ∈ relMod A := by
    have hm := neg_mem (rel_of_iso e)
    convert hm using 1
    abel
  have key : gammaA P = gammaA Q ↔
      -(FreeAbelianGroup.of P) + FreeAbelianGroup.of Q ∈ relMod A := by
    simp only [gammaA]
    exact QuotientAddGroup.eq
  exact key.mpr h'

theorem gamma_ses {P Q R : FinMod A} (s : SES (A := A) P Q R) :
    gammaA Q = gammaA P + gammaA R := by
  have h := rel_of_ses s
  rw [sub_sub] at h
  have h' : -(FreeAbelianGroup.of Q) + (FreeAbelianGroup.of P + FreeAbelianGroup.of R) ∈
      relMod A := by
    have hm := neg_mem h
    convert hm using 1
    abel
  have key : gammaA Q = gammaA P + gammaA R ↔
      -(FreeAbelianGroup.of Q) + (FreeAbelianGroup.of P + FreeAbelianGroup.of R) ∈ relMod A := by
    rw [show gammaA P + gammaA R =
      ((FreeAbelianGroup.of P + FreeAbelianGroup.of R : FreeAbelianGroup (FinMod A)) : K A)
        from rfl]
    simp only [gammaA]
    exact QuotientAddGroup.eq
  exact key.mpr h'

/-- Induction principle for `K(A)`. -/
theorem induction {p : K A → Prop} (hgen : ∀ M : FinMod A, p (gammaA M)) (h0 : p 0)
    (hneg : ∀ x, p x → p (-x)) (hadd : ∀ x y, p x → p y → p (x + y)) : ∀ x, p x := by
  intro x
  refine Quotient.inductionOn x fun a => ?_
  refine FreeAbelianGroup.induction_on a ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_
  · simpa using h0
  · intro M
    simpa [gammaA] using hgen M
  · intro M ih
    simpa [gammaA] using hneg (QuotientAddGroup.mk' (relMod A) (FreeAbelianGroup.of M)) ih
  · intro a b iha ihb
    simpa using hadd (QuotientAddGroup.mk' (relMod A) a) (QuotientAddGroup.mk' (relMod A) b)
      iha ihb

end K

/-- Auxiliary form of `liftFunMod`. -/
noncomputable def liftAuxMod {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {β : Type v} [AddCommGroup β]
    (φ : FinMod A → β) (h : relMod A ≤ (FreeAbelianGroup.lift φ).ker) : K A →+ β :=
  QuotientAddGroup.lift (relMod A) (FreeAbelianGroup.lift φ) h

theorem liftAuxMod_gamma {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {β : Type v} [AddCommGroup β]
    (φ : FinMod A → β) (h : relMod A ≤ (FreeAbelianGroup.lift φ).ker) (M : FinMod A) :
    liftAuxMod φ h (gammaA M) = φ M := by
  have h1 := QuotientAddGroup.lift_comp_mk' (relMod A) (FreeAbelianGroup.lift φ) h
  have h2 := DFunLike.congr_fun h1 (FreeAbelianGroup.of M)
  simpa only [liftAuxMod, gammaA, AddMonoidHom.comp_apply, FreeAbelianGroup.lift_apply_of] using h2

/-- **Universal property of `K(A)`.** -/
noncomputable def liftFunMod {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {β : Type v} [AddCommGroup β]
    (φ : FinMod A → β)
    (hiso : ∀ (P Q : FinMod A), Nonempty (P ≃ₗ[A] Q) → φ P = φ Q)
    (hses : ∀ (P Q R : FinMod A) (_ : SES (A := A) P Q R), φ Q = φ P + φ R) :
    K A →+ β :=
  liftAuxMod φ (by
    refine (AddSubgroup.closure_le _).mpr ?_
    rintro x (⟨P, Q, ⟨e⟩, rfl⟩ | ⟨P, Q, R, s, rfl⟩)
    · change FreeAbelianGroup.lift φ (FreeAbelianGroup.of P - FreeAbelianGroup.of Q) = 0
      rw [map_sub, FreeAbelianGroup.lift_apply_of, FreeAbelianGroup.lift_apply_of,
        hiso P Q ⟨e⟩, sub_self]
    · change FreeAbelianGroup.lift φ (FreeAbelianGroup.of Q - FreeAbelianGroup.of P -
        FreeAbelianGroup.of R) = 0
      have h := hses P Q R s
      rw [sub_sub, map_sub, map_add, FreeAbelianGroup.lift_apply_of,
        FreeAbelianGroup.lift_apply_of, FreeAbelianGroup.lift_apply_of, h]
      abel)

theorem liftFunMod_gamma {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {β : Type v} [AddCommGroup β]
    (φ : FinMod A → β)
    (hiso : ∀ (P Q : FinMod A), Nonempty (P ≃ₗ[A] Q) → φ P = φ Q)
    (hses : ∀ (P Q R : FinMod A) (_ : SES (A := A) P Q R), φ Q = φ P + φ R) (M : FinMod A) :
    liftFunMod φ hiso hses (gammaA M) = φ M :=
  liftAuxMod_gamma φ _ M

/-- Two additive maps out of `K(A)` agree if they agree on the generators `γ_A(M)`. -/
theorem hom_ext_K {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {β : Type v} [AddCommGroup β]
    {ψ₁ ψ₂ : K A →+ β} (h : ∀ M : FinMod A, ψ₁ (gammaA M) = ψ₂ (gammaA M)) : ψ₁ = ψ₂ := by
  refine AddMonoidHom.ext fun x => ?_
  refine Quotient.inductionOn x fun a => ?_
  refine FreeAbelianGroup.induction_on a ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_
  · simp
  · intro M
    simpa [gammaA] using h M
  · intro M ih
    simpa using congrArg Neg.neg ih
  · intro a b iha ihb
    simpa using congrArg₂ (fun z w => z + w) iha ihb

/-! ## Part (ii): `K(A)` is a module over `K₁(A)` -/

/-- Tensoring a short exact sequence of f.g. flat modules on the right with an arbitrary
finitely generated module gives a short exact sequence of finitely generated modules. -/
theorem gammaA_tensor_ses_right {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {P₁ P₂ P₃ : FinFlat A}
    (s : SES (A := A) P₁.toMod P₂.toMod P₃.toMod) (Q : FinMod A) :
    gammaA (FinMod.tensor P₂.toMod Q) = gammaA (FinMod.tensor P₁.toMod Q) +
      gammaA (FinMod.tensor P₃.toMod Q) := by
  have : Module.Flat A P₃.toMod.X := P₃.flat
  exact K.gamma_ses (P := FinMod.tensor P₁.toMod Q) (Q := FinMod.tensor P₂.toMod Q)
    (R := FinMod.tensor P₃.toMod Q)
    { f := s.f.rTensor Q
      g := s.g.rTensor Q
      inj := (LinearMap.lTensor_inj_iff_rTensor_inj Q s.f).mp
        (LinearMap.lTensor_injective_of_exact_of_flat s.g s.surj s.f s.inj s.exact Q)
      surj := LinearMap.rTensor_surjective Q s.surj
      exact := _root_.rTensor_exact Q s.exact s.surj }

/-- Tensoring a short exact sequence of f.g. modules on the left with a f.g. flat module gives a
short exact sequence of finitely generated modules. -/
theorem gammaA_tensor_ses_left {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (P : FinFlat A) {Q₁ Q₂ Q₃ : FinMod A}
    (s : SES (A := A) Q₁ Q₂ Q₃) :
    gammaA (FinMod.tensor P.toMod Q₂) = gammaA (FinMod.tensor P.toMod Q₁) +
      gammaA (FinMod.tensor P.toMod Q₃) :=
  K.gamma_ses (P := FinMod.tensor P.toMod Q₁) (Q := FinMod.tensor P.toMod Q₂)
    (R := FinMod.tensor P.toMod Q₃)
    { f := s.f.lTensor P
      g := s.g.lTensor P
      inj := Module.Flat.lTensor_preserves_injective_linearMap s.f s.inj
      surj := LinearMap.lTensor_surjective P s.surj
      exact := Module.Flat.lTensor_exact P s.exact }

section ModuleStructure

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A]

/-- The action of `γ₁(P)` on `K(A)`: multiplication by the class of `P`. -/
noncomputable def actLeft (P : FinFlat A) : K A →+ K A :=
  liftFunMod (fun M => gammaA (FinMod.tensor P.toMod M))
    (fun _ _ ⟨e⟩ => K.gamma_congr (TensorProduct.congr (LinearEquiv.refl A P) e))
    (fun _ _ _ s => gammaA_tensor_ses_left P s)

theorem actLeft_gamma (P : FinFlat A) (M : FinMod A) :
    actLeft P (gammaA M) = gammaA (FinMod.tensor P.toMod M) :=
  liftFunMod_gamma _ _ _ M

/-- The curried action, additive in the `K₁(A)`-variable. -/
noncomputable def act : K1 A →+ (K A →+ K A) :=
  liftFun (fun P => actLeft P)
    (fun _ _ ⟨e⟩ => hom_ext_K fun M => by
      rw [show actLeft _ (gammaA M) = gammaA (FinMod.tensor _ M) from actLeft_gamma _ M,
        show actLeft _ (gammaA M) = gammaA (FinMod.tensor _ M) from actLeft_gamma _ M]
      exact K.gamma_congr (TensorProduct.congr e (LinearEquiv.refl A M)))
    (fun _ _ _ s => hom_ext_K fun M => by
      rw [AddMonoidHom.add_apply,
        show actLeft _ (gammaA M) = gammaA (FinMod.tensor _ M) from actLeft_gamma _ M,
        show actLeft _ (gammaA M) = gammaA (FinMod.tensor _ M) from actLeft_gamma _ M,
        show actLeft _ (gammaA M) = gammaA (FinMod.tensor _ M) from actLeft_gamma _ M]
      exact gammaA_tensor_ses_right s M)

/-- The scalar multiplication of `K₁(A)` on `K(A)`. -/
noncomputable instance instSMul : SMul (K1 A) (K A) := ⟨fun x m => act x m⟩

theorem smul_gamma_gammaA (P : FinFlat A) (M : FinMod A) :
    gamma P • gammaA M = gammaA (FinMod.tensor P.toMod M) := by
  show act (gamma P) (gammaA M) = _
  have h : act (gamma P) = actLeft P := liftFun_gamma (fun P => actLeft P) _ _ P
  rw [h]
  exact actLeft_gamma P M

@[simp] theorem smul_add (x : K1 A) (m n : K A) : x • (m + n) = x • m + x • n :=
  map_add (act x) m n

@[simp] theorem smul_zero (x : K1 A) : x • (0 : K A) = 0 := map_zero (act x)

@[simp] theorem smul_neg (x : K1 A) (m : K A) : x • (-m) = -(x • m) := map_neg (act x) m

@[simp] theorem add_smul (x y : K1 A) (m : K A) : (x + y) • m = x • m + y • m := by
  show act (x + y) m = act x m + act y m
  rw [map_add]
  rfl

@[simp] theorem neg_smul (x : K1 A) (m : K A) : (-x) • m = -(x • m) := by
  show act (-x) m = -(act x m)
  rw [map_neg]
  rfl

@[simp] theorem smul_sub (x : K1 A) (m n : K A) : x • (m - n) = x • m - x • n :=
  map_sub (act x) m n

@[simp] theorem sub_smul (x y : K1 A) (m : K A) : (x - y) • m = x • m - y • m := by
  show act (x - y) m = act x m - act y m
  rw [map_sub]
  rfl

@[simp] theorem zero_smul (m : K A) : (0 : K1 A) • m = 0 := by
  show act 0 m = 0
  rw [map_zero]
  rfl

theorem one_smul (m : K A) : (1 : K1 A) • m = m := by
  induction m using K.induction with
  | hgen M =>
    rw [show (1 : K1 A) = gamma (FinFlat.ofSelf) from rfl, smul_gamma_gammaA]
    exact K.gamma_congr (TensorProduct.lid A M)
  | h0 => simp
  | hneg m ih => simp [ih]
  | hadd m₁ m₂ ih₁ ih₂ => simp [ih₁, ih₂]

theorem mul_smul (x y : K1 A) (m : K A) : (x * y) • m = x • (y • m) := by
  induction m using K.induction with
  | hgen M =>
    induction x using K1.induction with
    | hgen P =>
      induction y using K1.induction with
      | hgen Q =>
        rw [show gamma P * gamma Q = gamma (FinFlat.tensor P Q) from mul_gamma P Q,
          smul_gamma_gammaA, smul_gamma_gammaA, smul_gamma_gammaA]
        exact K.gamma_congr (TensorProduct.assoc A P Q M)
      | h0 => simp
      | hneg y ih => simp [ih]
      | hadd y₁ y₂ ih₁ ih₂ => simp [ih₁, ih₂]
    | h0 => simp
    | hneg x ih => simp [ih]
    | hadd x₁ x₂ ih₁ ih₂ => simp [ih₁, ih₂]
  | h0 => simp
  | hneg m ih => simp [ih]
  | hadd m₁ m₂ ih₁ ih₂ => simp [ih₁, ih₂]

/-- Part (ii): `K(A)` is a module over the ring `K₁(A)`, with `γ₁(P) • γ_A(M) = γ_A(P ⊗ M)`. -/
noncomputable instance instModule : Module (K1 A) (K A) where
  smul := (· • ·)
  one_smul := one_smul
  mul_smul := mul_smul
  smul_zero := smul_zero
  smul_add := smul_add
  add_smul := add_smul
  zero_smul := zero_smul

end ModuleStructure


/-! ## Part (iii): for a Noetherian local ring, `K₁(A) ≃ ℤ` -/

section PiA

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A]

/-- The free module `A^n`, as a finitely generated flat module. -/
noncomputable abbrev piA (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (n : ℕ) : FinFlat A :=
  ⟨Fin n → A, inferInstance, inferInstance⟩

/-- The inclusion `A^n → A^{n+1}` as the first `n` coordinates. -/
noncomputable def snocLM (n : ℕ) : (Fin n → A) →ₗ[A] (Fin (n + 1) → A) :=
  { toFun := fun v => Fin.snoc v 0
    map_add' := by
      intro a b
      funext i
      refine Fin.lastCases ?_ ?_ i <;> simp
    map_smul' := by
      intro a b
      funext i
      refine Fin.lastCases ?_ ?_ i <;> simp }

/-- The short exact sequence `0 → A^n → A^{n+1} → A → 0`. -/
noncomputable def piA_ses (n : ℕ) : SES (A := A) (piA A n).toMod (piA A (n + 1)).toMod
    (FinFlat.ofSelf (A := A)).toMod :=
  { f := snocLM n
    g := LinearMap.proj (R := A) (φ := fun _ => A) (Fin.last n)
    inj := by
      intro u v huv
      funext i
      have h := congrFun huv (Fin.castSucc i)
      simpa [snocLM] using h
    surj := by
      intro a
      exact ⟨Fin.snoc (0 : Fin n → A) a, by simp⟩
    exact := by
      rw [LinearMap.exact_iff]
      refine SetLike.ext fun w => ?_
      constructor
      · intro hw
        rw [LinearMap.mem_ker] at hw
        have hw' : w (Fin.last n) = 0 := by simpa using hw
        refine ⟨Fin.init w, ?_⟩
        show Fin.snoc (Fin.init w) (0 : A) = w
        have h1 : Fin.snoc (Fin.init w) (0 : A) = Fin.snoc (Fin.init w) (w (Fin.last n)) := by
          rw [hw']
        rw [h1, Fin.snoc_init_self]
      · rintro ⟨v, rfl⟩
        rw [LinearMap.mem_ker]
        have h1 : (snocLM n) v (Fin.last n) = 0 := by simp [snocLM]
        simpa using h1 }

theorem gamma_piA_succ (n : ℕ) :
    gamma (piA A (n + 1)) = gamma (piA A n) + gamma (FinFlat.ofSelf) :=
  K1.gamma_ses (piA_ses n)

theorem gamma_piA_one : gamma (piA A 1) = gamma (FinFlat.ofSelf (A := A)) :=
  K1.gamma_congr (LinearEquiv.funUnique (Fin 1) A A)

theorem gamma_piA_zsmul (n : ℕ) : gamma (piA A n) = (n : ℤ) • (1 : K1 A) := by
  induction n with
  | zero =>
    have h1 : gamma (piA A 0) + gamma (FinFlat.ofSelf) = 0 + gamma (FinFlat.ofSelf) := by
      rw [zero_add, ← gamma_piA_succ 0, gamma_piA_one]
    exact add_right_cancel h1
  | succ n ih =>
    rw [gamma_piA_succ, ih, show gamma (FinFlat.ofSelf (A := A)) = 1 from rfl]
    push_cast
    ring

/-- The rank of a f.g. flat module, as an integer. -/
noncomputable abbrev rankFn (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (P : FinFlat A) : ℤ :=
  (Module.finrank A P.X : ℤ)

theorem rankFn_congr {P Q : FinFlat A} (e : P ≃ₗ[A] Q) : rankFn A P = rankFn A Q := by
  have h : Module.finrank A P.X = Module.finrank A Q.X := e.finrank_eq
  simp only [rankFn, h]

end PiA

section Local

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A]

/-- In a short exact sequence of f.g. flat modules over a local ring the rank of the middle
term is the sum of the ranks of the outer terms (a short exact sequence of free modules
splits). -/
theorem finrank_ses {P Q R : FinFlat A}
    (s : SES (A := A) P.toMod Q.toMod R.toMod) :
    Module.finrank A Q.X = Module.finrank A P.X + Module.finrank A R.X := by
  have hP : Module.Free A P.X := Module.free_of_flat_of_isLocalRing
  have hQ : Module.Free A Q.X := Module.free_of_flat_of_isLocalRing
  have hR : Module.Free A R.X := Module.free_of_flat_of_isLocalRing
  have hRproj : Module.Projective A R.X := Module.Projective.of_free
  obtain ⟨h, hh⟩ := LinearMap.exists_rightInverse_of_surjective s.g
    (LinearMap.range_eq_top_of_surjective s.g s.surj)
  have hgh : ∀ r : R.X, s.g (h r) = r := fun r => LinearMap.congr_fun hh r
  have hgf : ∀ p : P.X, s.g (s.f p) = 0 := by
    intro p
    have h0 := LinearMap.congr_fun (Function.Exact.linearMap_comp_eq_zero s.exact) p
    simpa using h0
  have hker : ∀ x : Q.X, s.g x = 0 → ∃ p, s.f p = x := by
    intro x hx
    have h1 : x ∈ LinearMap.range s.f := by
      rw [← LinearMap.exact_iff.mp s.exact]
      exact hx
    exact h1
  let ψ : P.X × R.X →ₗ[A] Q.X :=
    s.f.comp (LinearMap.fst A P.X R.X) + h.comp (LinearMap.snd A P.X R.X)
  have hψ_apply : ∀ pr : P.X × R.X, ψ pr = s.f pr.1 + h pr.2 := fun pr => rfl
  have hψ : Function.Bijective ψ := by
    constructor
    · intro u v huv
      have huv' : s.f u.1 + h u.2 = s.f v.1 + h v.2 := huv
      have h2 : u.2 = v.2 := by
        have h1 : s.g (ψ u) = s.g (ψ v) := by rw [huv]
        simpa [hψ_apply, hgf, hgh] using h1
      have h3 : s.f u.1 = s.f v.1 := by
        rw [h2, add_left_inj] at huv'
        exact huv'
      exact Prod.ext (s.inj h3) h2
    · intro x
      obtain ⟨p, hp⟩ := hker (x - h (s.g x)) (by rw [map_sub, hgh, sub_self])
      refine ⟨(p, s.g x), ?_⟩
      rw [hψ_apply, hp]
      abel
  have hfin : Module.finrank A Q.X = Module.finrank A (P.X × R.X) :=
    (LinearEquiv.ofBijective ψ hψ).finrank_eq.symm
  rw [hfin, Module.finrank_prod]

theorem rankFn_ses {P Q R : FinFlat A} (s : SES (A := A) P.toMod Q.toMod R.toMod) :
    rankFn A Q = rankFn A P + rankFn A R := by
  simp only [rankFn]
  rw [finrank_ses s]
  push_cast
  ring

/-- The rank gives an additive map `K₁(A) → ℤ`. -/
noncomputable def rankHom : K1 A →+ ℤ :=
  liftFun (fun P => rankFn A P) (fun _ _ ⟨e⟩ => rankFn_congr e) (fun _ _ _ s => rankFn_ses s)

theorem rankHom_gamma (P : FinFlat A) : rankHom (gamma P) = rankFn A P :=
  liftFun_gamma _ _ _ P

theorem rankFn_tensor (P Q : FinFlat A) :
    rankFn A (FinFlat.tensor P Q) = rankFn A P * rankFn A Q := by
  have hP : Module.Free A P.X := Module.free_of_flat_of_isLocalRing
  have hQ : Module.Free A Q.X := Module.free_of_flat_of_isLocalRing
  have hPQ : Module.Free A (P.X ⊗[A] Q.X) := inferInstance
  simp only [rankFn, FinFlat.tensor]
  rw [Module.finrank_tensorProduct]
  push_cast
  ring

theorem rankHom_one : rankHom (1 : K1 A) = 1 := by
  show rankHom (gamma (FinFlat.ofSelf)) = 1
  rw [rankHom_gamma]
  simp [rankFn, FinFlat.ofSelf]

theorem rankHom_mul (x y : K1 A) : rankHom (x * y) = rankHom x * rankHom y := by
  induction x using K1.induction with
  | hgen P =>
    induction y using K1.induction with
    | hgen Q =>
      rw [show gamma P * gamma Q = gamma (FinFlat.tensor P Q) from mul_gamma P Q,
        rankHom_gamma, rankHom_gamma, rankHom_gamma, rankFn_tensor]
    | h0 => simp
    | hneg y ih => simp [ih]
    | hadd y₁ y₂ ih₁ ih₂ =>
      rw [mul_add', map_add, ih₁, ih₂, map_add, _root_.mul_add]
  | h0 => simp
  | hneg x ih => simp [ih]
  | hadd x₁ x₂ ih₁ ih₂ =>
    rw [add_mul', map_add, ih₁, ih₂, map_add, _root_.add_mul]

/-- The rank as a ring homomorphism `K₁(A) → ℤ`. -/
noncomputable def rankRingHom : K1 A →+* ℤ :=
  { rankHom with map_one' := rankHom_one, map_mul' := rankHom_mul }

theorem gamma_eq_zsmul_one (P : FinFlat A) :
    gamma P = (Module.finrank A P.X : ℤ) • (1 : K1 A) := by
  have hP : Module.Free A P.X := Module.free_of_flat_of_isLocalRing
  have h1 : gamma P = gamma (piA A (Module.finrank A P.X)) :=
    K1.gamma_congr (Module.finBasis A P.X).equivFun
  rw [h1, gamma_piA_zsmul]

theorem rankRingHom_bijective : Function.Bijective (rankRingHom (A := A)) := by
  have key : ∀ x : K1 A, x = (rankHom x) • (1 : K1 A) := by
    intro x
    induction x using K1.induction with
    | hgen P => exact gamma_eq_zsmul_one P
    | h0 => simp
    | hneg x ih =>
      rw [map_neg, neg_zsmul, ← ih]
    | hadd x₁ x₂ ih₁ ih₂ =>
      rw [map_add, add_zsmul, ← ih₁, ← ih₂]
  constructor
  · intro x y hxy
    have hxy' : rankHom x = rankHom y := hxy
    rw [key x, key y, hxy']
  · intro n
    refine ⟨n • (1 : K1 A), ?_⟩
    show rankHom (n • (1 : K1 A)) = n
    rw [map_zsmul, rankHom_one, smul_eq_mul, _root_.mul_one]

/-- Part (iii): for a Noetherian local ring `A`, the rank gives a ring isomorphism
`K₁(A) ≃ ℤ`, sending `γ₁(A)` to `1`. -/
noncomputable def rankEquiv : K1 A ≃+* ℤ :=
  RingEquiv.ofBijective rankRingHom rankRingHom_bijective

theorem rankEquiv_symm_apply (n : ℤ) : (rankEquiv (A := A)).symm n = n • (1 : K1 A) := by
  apply (rankEquiv (A := A)).injective
  rw [RingEquiv.apply_symm_apply]
  show n = rankHom (n • (1 : K1 A))
  rw [map_zsmul, rankHom_one, smul_eq_mul, _root_.mul_one]

/-- Part (iii): for a Noetherian local ring `A` there is a ring isomorphism `K₁(A) ≃ ℤ`
sending `γ₁(A)` to `1`. -/
theorem exists_ringEquiv_int [IsNoetherianRing A] :
    ∃ e : K1 A ≃+* ℤ, e (gamma (FinFlat.ofSelf (A := A))) = 1 := by
  refine ⟨rankEquiv, ?_⟩
  show rankHom (gamma (FinFlat.ofSelf (A := A))) = 1
  rw [rankHom_gamma]
  simp [rankFn, FinFlat.ofSelf]

end Local


/-! ## Part (iv): extension of scalars induces a ring homomorphism `K₁(A) → K₁(B)` -/

section BaseChange

variable {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]

/-- Extension of scalars `P ↦ B ⊗_A P` of a f.g. flat module. -/
noncomputable abbrev extScalar (P : FinFlat A) : FinFlat B :=
  ⟨B ⊗[A] P.X, Module.Finite.base_change A B P.X, inferInstance⟩

theorem gamma_extScalar_congr {P Q : FinFlat A} (e : P ≃ₗ[A] Q) :
    gamma (extScalar (B := B) P) = gamma (extScalar (B := B) Q) :=
  K1.gamma_congr (LinearEquiv.baseChange A B P.X Q.X e)

theorem gamma_extScalar_ses {P Q R : FinFlat A}
    (s : SES (A := A) P.toMod Q.toMod R.toMod) :
    gamma (extScalar (B := B) Q) = gamma (extScalar (B := B) P) +
      gamma (extScalar (B := B) R) :=
  K1.gamma_ses (P := extScalar (B := B) P) (Q := extScalar (B := B) Q)
    (R := extScalar (B := B) R)
    { f := TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.lTensor (A := B) (M := B) s.f
      g := TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.lTensor (A := B) (M := B) s.g
      inj := LinearMap.lTensor_injective_of_exact_of_flat s.g s.surj s.f s.inj s.exact B
      surj := LinearMap.lTensor_surjective B s.surj
      exact := _root_.lTensor_exact B s.exact s.surj }

/-- Extension of scalars is additive on `K₁`. -/
noncomputable def baseChangeAdd : K1 A →+ K1 B :=
  liftFun (fun P => gamma (extScalar (B := B) P))
    (fun _ _ ⟨e⟩ => gamma_extScalar_congr e) (fun _ _ _ s => gamma_extScalar_ses s)

theorem baseChangeAdd_gamma (P : FinFlat A) :
    baseChangeAdd (A := A) (B := B) (gamma P) = gamma (extScalar (B := B) P) :=
  liftFun_gamma _ _ _ P

theorem baseChangeAdd_one : baseChangeAdd (A := A) (B := B) 1 = 1 := by
  show baseChangeAdd (A := A) (B := B) (gamma (FinFlat.ofSelf)) = 1
  rw [baseChangeAdd_gamma]
  exact K1.gamma_congr (TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.rid A B B)

theorem baseChangeAdd_mul (x y : K1 A) :
    baseChangeAdd (A := A) (B := B) (x * y) =
      baseChangeAdd (A := A) (B := B) x * baseChangeAdd (A := A) (B := B) y := by
  induction x using K1.induction with
  | hgen P =>
    induction y using K1.induction with
    | hgen Q =>
      rw [show gamma P * gamma Q = gamma (FinFlat.tensor P Q) from mul_gamma P Q,
        baseChangeAdd_gamma, baseChangeAdd_gamma, baseChangeAdd_gamma,
        gamma_mul_gamma (A := B)]
      exact K1.gamma_congr ((TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.cancelBaseChange A B B
        (B ⊗[A] P.X) Q.X).trans
          (TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.assoc A A B B P.X Q.X)).symm
    | h0 => simp
    | hneg y ih => simp [ih]
    | hadd y₁ y₂ ih₁ ih₂ =>
      rw [mul_add', map_add, ih₁, ih₂, map_add, _root_.mul_add]
  | h0 => simp
  | hneg x ih => simp [ih]
  | hadd x₁ x₂ ih₁ ih₂ =>
    rw [add_mul', map_add, ih₁, ih₂, map_add, _root_.add_mul]

/-- **Part (iv)**: a ring homomorphism `A → B` (i.e. an `A`-algebra structure on `B`) induces a
ring homomorphism `f^! : K₁(A) → K₁(B)` with `f^!(γ₁(P)) = γ₁(B ⊗_A P)`. -/
noncomputable def baseChangeHom : K1 A →+* K1 B :=
  { baseChangeAdd with
    map_one' := baseChangeAdd_one
    map_mul' := baseChangeAdd_mul }

theorem baseChangeHom_gamma (P : FinFlat A) :
    baseChangeHom (A := A) (B := B) (gamma P) = gamma (extScalar (B := B) P) :=
  baseChangeAdd_gamma P

end BaseChange


/-! ### Functoriality of `f^!` -/

section Functoriality

variable {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]

/-- The composition formula `(g ∘ f)^! = g^! ∘ f^!` for extension of scalars. -/
theorem baseChangeHom_comp {C : Type u} [CommRing C] [Algebra B C] [Algebra A C]
    [IsScalarTower A B C] :
    (baseChangeHom (A := A) (B := C)) =
      (baseChangeHom (A := B) (B := C)).comp (baseChangeHom (A := A) (B := B)) := by
  refine RingHom.ext fun x => ?_
  induction x using K1.induction with
  | hgen P =>
    rw [RingHom.comp_apply, baseChangeHom_gamma, baseChangeHom_gamma, baseChangeHom_gamma]
    exact (K1.gamma_congr
      (TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.cancelBaseChange A B C C P.X)).symm
  | h0 => simp
  | hneg x ih => simp [ih]
  | hadd x₁ x₂ ih₁ ih₂ => simp [ih₁, ih₂]

end Functoriality

/-! ## Part (v): restriction of scalars and the projection formula -/

section Restrict

variable {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] [Module.Finite A B]

/-- Bundle a type with a specified module structure (the instance is an explicit argument). -/
abbrev mkFinMod (X : Type u) [AddCommGroup X] [Module A X] (f : Module.Finite A X) : FinMod A :=
  ⟨X, f⟩

/-- Changing the `Module` structure of a bundle along an equality of module structures does not
change its class in `K(A)`. -/
theorem gammaA_congr_module {X : Type u} [AddCommGroup X] {m₁ m₂ : Module A X} (h : m₁ = m₂)
    (f : @Module.Finite A X _ _ m₁) :
    gammaA (@mkFinMod A _ X _ m₁ f) = gammaA (@mkFinMod A _ X _ m₂ (h ▸ f)) := by
  subst h
  rfl

/-- The `A`-module structure on a f.g. `B`-module, restricted along the algebra map `A → B`. -/
instance instModuleRestrictMod (M : FinMod B) : Module A M.X :=
  Module.compHom M.X (algebraMap A B)

instance instIsScalarTowerRestrictMod (M : FinMod B) : IsScalarTower A B M.X :=
  IsScalarTower.of_compHom A B M.X

/-- A `B`-linear map is `A`-linear for the restricted module structure. -/
noncomputable def restrictLinMap (M N : Type u) [AddCommGroup M] [AddCommGroup N]
    [Module B M] [Module B N] [Module A M] [Module A N] [IsScalarTower A B M]
    [IsScalarTower A B N] (f : M →ₗ[B] N) : M →ₗ[A] N :=
  { toFun := f
    map_add' := f.map_add
    map_smul' := fun a m => by
      rw [← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_smul B a m, f.map_smul,
        IsScalarTower.algebraMap_smul B a (f m)]
      rfl }

/-- A `B`-linear equivalence is `A`-linear for the restricted module structure. -/
noncomputable def restrictLinEquiv (M N : Type u) [AddCommGroup M] [AddCommGroup N]
    [Module B M] [Module B N] [Module A M] [Module A N] [IsScalarTower A B M]
    [IsScalarTower A B N] (e : M ≃ₗ[B] N) : M ≃ₗ[A] N :=
  { restrictLinMap M N e.toLinearMap with
    invFun := e.symm
    left_inv := e.left_inv
    right_inv := e.right_inv }

/-- Restriction of scalars along a finite algebra map, on finitely generated modules: a finitely
generated `B`-module is a finitely generated `A`-module. -/
noncomputable abbrev resScalarMod (M : FinMod B) : FinMod A :=
  ⟨M.X, Module.Finite.trans (R := A) (A := B) (M := M.X)⟩

theorem gammaA_resScalarMod_congr {M N : FinMod B} (e : M ≃ₗ[B] N) :
    gammaA (resScalarMod (A := A) M) = gammaA (resScalarMod (A := A) N) :=
  K.gamma_congr (restrictLinEquiv (A := A) M.X N.X e)

theorem gammaA_resScalarMod_ses {P Q R : FinMod B} (s : SES (A := B) P Q R) :
    gammaA (resScalarMod (A := A) Q) =
      gammaA (resScalarMod (A := A) P) + gammaA (resScalarMod (A := A) R) :=
  K.gamma_ses (P := resScalarMod (A := A) P) (Q := resScalarMod (A := A) Q)
    (R := resScalarMod (A := A) R)
    { f := restrictLinMap (A := A) P.X Q.X s.f
      g := restrictLinMap (A := A) Q.X R.X s.g
      inj := s.inj
      surj := s.surj
      exact := s.exact }

/-- **Part (v)**, the map `f_! : K(B) → K(A)`: restriction of scalars along a finite ring
homomorphism `f : A → B`, on classes given by `f_!(γ_B(N)) = γ_A(N)`. -/
noncomputable def resScalarK : K B →+ K A :=
  liftFunMod (fun M => gammaA (resScalarMod (A := A) M))
    (fun _ _ ⟨e⟩ => gammaA_resScalarMod_congr e) (fun _ _ _ s => gammaA_resScalarMod_ses s)

theorem resScalarK_gammaA (M : FinMod B) :
    resScalarK (A := A) (B := B) (gammaA M) = gammaA (resScalarMod (A := A) M) :=
  liftFunMod_gamma _ _ _ M

/-- **Part (v)**, the `K₁(A)`-module structure on `K(B)` obtained by restriction of scalars along
`f^! : K₁(A) → K₁(B)`. -/
noncomputable instance instModuleK1K : Module (K1 A) (K B) :=
  Module.compHom (K B) (baseChangeHom (A := A) (B := B))

omit [Module.Finite A B] in
theorem smul_K1A_def (x : K1 A) (y : K B) :
    x • y = baseChangeHom (A := A) (B := B) x • y := rfl

/-- For a tensor product over `B` of a `B`-module and a f.g. `B`-module, the `A`-module structure
obtained by restricting scalars coincides with the canonical left action of `A` on the left
factor. -/
theorem restrictModEqLeft (P : FinFlat A) (N : FinMod B) :
    (instModuleRestrictMod (FinMod.tensor (FinFlat.toMod (extScalar (B := B) P)) N)
      : Module A ((B ⊗[A] P.X) ⊗[B] N.X)) = TensorProduct.leftModule := by
  refine Module.ext' _ _ (fun a x => ?_)
  change (algebraMap A B a) • x = a • x
  exact IsScalarTower.algebraMap_smul (A := B) a x

/-- The comparison isomorphism `(B ⊗_A P) ⊗_B N ≅ P ⊗_A N` of `A`-modules (with `N` regarded as
an `A`-module by restriction of scalars): the isomorphism that turns the generator computation for
the projection formula into an equality of classes. -/
noncomputable def projectionIsoMod (P : FinFlat A) (N : FinMod B) :
    (resScalarMod (A := A)
        (FinMod.tensor (FinFlat.toMod (extScalar (B := B) P)) N)).X ≃ₗ[A]
      (FinMod.tensor P.toMod (resScalarMod (A := A) N)).X :=
  (restrictLinEquiv (A := A) ((B ⊗[A] P.X) ⊗[B] N.X) (N.X ⊗[B] (B ⊗[A] P.X))
      (TensorProduct.comm B (B ⊗[A] P.X) N.X)).trans
    ((restrictLinEquiv (A := A) (N.X ⊗[B] (B ⊗[A] P.X)) (N.X ⊗[A] P.X)
      (TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.cancelBaseChange A B B N.X P.X)).trans
      (TensorProduct.comm A N.X P.X))

/-- The generator computation for the projection formula: the classes of `(B ⊗_A P) ⊗_B N` and of
`P ⊗_A N` in `K(A)` coincide. -/
theorem gammaA_projection (P : FinFlat A) (N : FinMod B) :
    gammaA (resScalarMod (A := A) (FinMod.tensor (FinFlat.toMod (extScalar (B := B) P)) N)) =
      gammaA (FinMod.tensor P.toMod (resScalarMod (A := A) N)) := by
  have hfin : @Module.Finite A ((B ⊗[A] P.X) ⊗[B] N.X) _ _
      (instModuleRestrictMod (FinMod.tensor (FinFlat.toMod (extScalar (B := B) P)) N)) :=
    (resScalarMod (A := A)
      (FinMod.tensor (FinFlat.toMod (extScalar (B := B) P)) N)).fin
  have h1 : gammaA (resScalarMod (A := A)
        (FinMod.tensor (FinFlat.toMod (extScalar (B := B) P)) N)) =
      gammaA (@mkFinMod A _ ((B ⊗[A] P.X) ⊗[B] N.X) _ TensorProduct.leftModule
        (restrictModEqLeft (A := A) P N ▸ hfin)) :=
    gammaA_congr_module (restrictModEqLeft (A := A) P N) hfin
  rw [h1]
  exact K.gamma_congr (projectionIsoMod P N)

/-- **Part (v)**: the projection formula `f_!(f^!(x) · y) = x · f_!(y)` for a finite ring
homomorphism `f : A → B`, `x ∈ K₁(A)` and `y ∈ K(B)`; here `K(B)` carries the `K₁(A)`-module
structure obtained by restricting scalars along `f^!`. -/
theorem projection_formula (x : K1 A) (y : K B) :
    resScalarK (A := A) (B := B) (x • y) = x • resScalarK (A := A) (B := B) y := by
  induction x using K1.induction with
  | hgen P =>
    induction y using K.induction with
    | hgen N =>
      have h1 : (gamma P : K1 A) • (gammaA N : K B) =
          gammaA (FinMod.tensor (FinFlat.toMod (extScalar (B := B) P)) N) := by
        show baseChangeHom (A := A) (B := B) (gamma P) • (gammaA N) = _
        rw [baseChangeHom_gamma]
        exact smul_gamma_gammaA (A := B) (extScalar (B := B) P) N
      have h2 : (gamma P : K1 A) • resScalarK (A := A) (B := B) (gammaA N) =
          gammaA (FinMod.tensor P.toMod (resScalarMod (A := A) N)) := by
        rw [resScalarK_gammaA]
        exact smul_gamma_gammaA (A := A) P (resScalarMod (A := A) N)
      rw [h1, h2, resScalarK_gammaA]
      exact gammaA_projection P N
    | h0 => simp
    | hneg N ih => simp [_root_.smul_neg, map_neg, ih]
    | hadd N₁ N₂ ih₁ ih₂ => simp [_root_.smul_add, map_add, ih₁, ih₂]
  | h0 => simp
  | hneg x ih => simp [_root_.neg_smul, map_neg, ih]
  | hadd x₁ x₂ ih₁ ih₂ => simp [_root_.add_smul, map_add, ih₁, ih₂]

end Restrict


/-! ## Summary of the formalized assertions -/

section Summary

/-- **Part (i)**: `K₁(A)` is a commutative ring whose unit is the class `γ₁(A)` of the free
module of rank one (see `gamma_self_eq_one`). -/
@[instance_reducible]
noncomputable def part_i (A : Type u) [CommRing A] : CommRing (K1 A) := inferInstance

/-- **Part (ii)**: `K(A)` is a module over `K₁(A)` (see `smul_gamma_gammaA` for the action of a
class `γ₁(P)`). -/
@[instance_reducible]
noncomputable def part_ii (A : Type u) [CommRing A] : Module (K1 A) (K A) := inferInstance

/-- **Part (i)**, on the generators: multiplication is induced by the tensor product, the unit is
the class of the free module of rank one, and the multiplication is commutative and associative. -/
theorem part_i_spec (A : Type u) [CommRing A] :
    (∀ P Q : FinFlat A, gamma P * gamma Q = gamma (FinFlat.tensor P Q)) ∧
      (1 : K1 A) = gamma (FinFlat.ofSelf (A := A)) ∧
      (∀ x y : K1 A, x * y = y * x) ∧
      (∀ x y z : K1 A, x * y * z = x * (y * z)) :=
  ⟨fun P Q => mul_gamma P Q, rfl, fun x y => mul_comm x y, fun x y z => mul_assoc x y z⟩

/-- **Part (ii)**, on the generators: `K(A)` is a module over the ring `K₁(A)` with
`γ₁(P) • γ_A(M) = γ_A(P ⊗_A M)`, compatible with the ring structure of `K₁(A)`. -/
theorem part_ii_spec (A : Type u) [CommRing A] :
    (∀ (P : FinFlat A) (M : FinMod A),
        gamma P • gammaA M = gammaA (FinMod.tensor P.toMod M)) ∧
      (∀ m : K A, (1 : K1 A) • m = m) ∧
      (∀ (x y : K1 A) (m : K A), (x * y) • m = x • (y • m)) :=
  ⟨fun P M => smul_gamma_gammaA P M, one_smul, mul_smul⟩

/-- **Part (iii)**: for a Noetherian local ring `A` there is a ring isomorphism `K₁(A) ≃ ℤ`
carrying `γ₁(A)` to `1`. -/
theorem part_iii (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] :
    ∃ e : K1 A ≃+* ℤ, e (gamma (FinFlat.ofSelf (A := A))) = 1 :=
  exists_ringEquiv_int

/-- **Part (iv)**: extension of scalars gives a ring homomorphism `f^! : K₁(A) → K₁(B)` with
`f^!(γ₁(P)) = γ₁(B ⊗_A P)` and `(g ∘ f)^! = g^! ∘ f^!`. -/
theorem part_iv (A B C : Type u) [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [CommRing C] [Algebra A B]
    [Algebra B C] [Algebra A C] [IsScalarTower A B C] :
    (∀ P : FinFlat A, baseChangeHom (A := A) (B := B) (gamma P) =
        gamma (extScalar (B := B) P)) ∧
      (baseChangeHom (A := A) (B := C) =
        (baseChangeHom (A := B) (B := C)).comp (baseChangeHom (A := A) (B := B))) :=
  ⟨fun P => baseChangeHom_gamma P, baseChangeHom_comp⟩

/-- **Part (v)**: for a finite ring homomorphism `f : A → B`, restriction of scalars gives
`f_! : K(B) → K(A)` with `f_!(γ_B(N)) = γ_A(N)`, `K(B)` is a `K₁(A)`-module along `f^!`, and the
projection formula `f_!(f^!(x) · y) = x · f_!(y)` holds for all `x ∈ K₁(A)`, `y ∈ K(B)`. -/
theorem part_v (A B : Type u) [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] [Module.Finite A B] :
    (∀ M : FinMod B, resScalarK (A := A) (B := B) (gammaA M)
        = gammaA (resScalarMod (A := A) M)) ∧
      (∀ (x : K1 A) (y : K B),
        resScalarK (A := A) (B := B) (x • y)
          = x • resScalarK (A := A) (B := B) y) :=
  ⟨fun M => resScalarK_gammaA M, fun x y => projection_formula x y⟩

end Summary

end AtiyahMcdonald69.Ex_7_27


